 "intro": "The upper valley of the Baetis (Guadalquivir), southern Spain, 211 BC. You are the brothers Publius and Gnaeus Cornelius Scipio, who have fought in Spain for seven years, against three Carthaginian armies.",
 "debrief": "In Livy’s account, the brothers split their forces. Gnaeus’s Celtiberian mercenaries were bribed to leave. Publius, harried by Masinissa’s Numidians, marched by night to stop Indibilis from joining them, was caught by the Carthaginian armies and killed. Gnaeus, retreating, was overtaken and made a last stand on a bare hill with baggage for a wall, and was killed too. The knight Lucius Marcius rallied the survivors north of the Ebro. The father and uncle of Scipio Africanus died within a month. The other choices are what-ifs.",
